@foolip @cdumez it means that in the future we can use IDL enumerations to define the attributes themselves as well and don't create weird differences in what values are accepted in attributes and APIs.

Or if in the future we move from an IDL enumeration to an open-ended value with user-supplied values, those would suddenly have to be ASCII case-insensitive as well because HTML stepped on the value space. 

Anyway, I said all this already I guess and my points keep being ignored.
